## 🔴 MAJOR PATTERN #1: source_not_found (3,063 — 69.3%)

**Systemic issue across ALL sub-agents.** Agents call `load(source="...")` with source names not registered in the delegation registry.

| Agent | Errors | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| **🦆 goose-expert** | **256** | Trying `load()` for non-existent instruction files |
| **🤖 GENERAL-IMPROVER** | **182** | Pipeline coordination — references missing source names |
| **🔍 im-finder** | **170** | Session scanning references unavailable sources |
| **✏️ yaml-editor** | **166** | Backup/patch operations reference missing files |
| **✅ im-validator** | **97** | Validation references unavailable instruction files |
| **🎨 im-designer** | **91** | Patch design references missing templates |
| **🪞 SELF-AUDITOR** | **84** | Audit references unavailable docs |
| **📊 im-rank** | **69** | Ranking references unavailable sources |
| **⏳ im-session-reader** | **51** | Session data references missing sources |
| **🚦 PRE-PUSH-VALIDATOR** | **53** | Pre-push checks reference unavailable files |

**⚡ Root cause:** Many `.md` instruction files and source names referenced via `load()` are not registered in `load()`'s available sources list. Common patterns: `load("recipe/instructions/sub_mas-xxx.md")` when the source name should be just `sub_mas-xxx`.

---

